<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Breadfield</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1479">1479</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Kenyérmező · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-hungarian-wars">Ottoman–Hungarian wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Breadfield (Kenyérmező) was fought on 13 October 1479 near Orăștie in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a>, where Hungarian forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephen-bathory">Stephen Báthory</a> and Paul Kinizsi destroyed a large Ottoman raiding army. It was the greatest Hungarian victory over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in the reign of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matthias-corvinus">Matthias Corvinus</a> and kept Transylvania free of major raids for years.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-breadfield.jpg" alt="Battle of Breadfield" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Eduard Gurk · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Keny%C3%A9rmez%C5%91i_csata.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
